---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {getLibrary} from '../lib/rebuild';
import copy from '../data/rebuild/copy-audit.json';
import exam from '../data/rebuild/exam-info.json';
import a from '../data/rebuild/case-details-a.json';
import b from '../data/rebuild/case-details-b.json';
import provisions from '../data/rebuild/provision-details.json';
import {sourceIndex,sourceStats} from '../lib/source-corpus';
const corpus=sourceIndex(),sourceAudit=sourceStats();
const cases=[...a.cases,...b.cases];
const library=await getLibrary();const gaps=cases.filter(c=>c.verification==='unresolved');
const count=(v:string)=>cases.filter(c=>c.verification===v).length;
---
<Layout title="Coverage & source audit" wide centre><p class="label">Nothing hidden</p><h1>Coverage & source audit</h1><p class="rb-lede">Inclusion, preserved source detail and independent verification are separate checks.</p><div class="rb-grid"><article class="rb-card"><h2>{copy.exactMatches.toLocaleString()} / {copy.checkedContentFiles.toLocaleString()}</h2><p>Original content files preserved byte for byte against source commit <span class="mono">{copy.sourceCommit.slice(0,12)}</span>.</p></article><article class="rb-card"><h2>77 / 77 case entries</h2><p>Every numbered entry in the Torts examinable list has an expanded dossier, two explanations, source trail and explicit limits. Companion decisions are recorded alongside their numbered entry.</p></article><article class="rb-card"><h2>45 / 45 provision entries</h2><p>Every list entry has full operative text, conditions, exceptions, application and two explanations. Subsection-only scope remains labelled.</p></article><article class="rb-card"><h2>11 / 11 supplied originals</h2><p>All images, transcripts, assessment HTML and Word documents are retained with checksums and accessible from Sources.</p></article></div>
<h2>Working-folder source coverage</h2>
{corpus.files.length>0?<><div class="rb-grid"><article class="rb-card"><h3>{sourceAudit.files.toLocaleString()} source records</h3><p>Original files are grouped by SHA-256 when their bytes are available. Each retained path and Drive link stays attached to its record.</p></article><article class="rb-card"><h3>{sourceAudit.sections.toLocaleString()} extracted sections</h3><p>{sourceAudit.characters.toLocaleString()} characters are available in full source views. Source text is rendered literally, including punctuation and section numbers.</p></article></div><p>{sourceAudit.flaggedFiles.toLocaleString()} source records carry extraction qualifications. Machine OCR, image-only material and original-only records remain labelled.</p><p>These counts establish inventory and extracted-text availability. They do not certify every image, diagram, recording or rewritten legal explanation letter by letter. Source views retain text and visuals for checking uncertain details directly.</p><p><a href="/source-corpus/index.json" download>Download source inventory and extraction evidence</a> · <a href="/sources/">Read every source record</a></p></>:<p>The working-folder extraction is being prepared; earlier retained repository sources remain available.</p>}
<h2>What the case verification means</h2><p>{count('primary-verified')} case entries were checked against primary judgments; {count('teaching-source')} rely on retained course records; {gaps.length} retain a specific unresolved factual or disposition detail. These flags are visible in the library and full dossier.</p><p>A complete list is not proof that a short course summary contains every fact in a judgment. Original teaching records are preserved for comparison; independently checked corrections appear above them. No missing fact is invented to make an audit look complete.</p>{gaps.map(c=><details class="rb-note"><summary>{c.listNumber}. {c.name} · detail needs checking</summary><p>{c.verificationNote}</p><a href={`/cases/${c.ref}/`}>Inspect source details and limits</a></details>)}
<h2>Legislation verification</h2><p>All 45 entries include complete operative text. The supplied Civil Liability Act PDF was cross-checked with a second extraction engine: 237 paragraphs and both publisher notes matched. Publisher notes are shown separately from operative law. The full sections include any surrounding text necessary to understand subsection-only exam scope.</p>{provisions.provisions.filter(p=>p.verification!=='primary-verified'||/inference|historical|403/i.test(p.verificationNote)).map(p=><details class="rb-note"><summary>{p.sourceLine}</summary><p>{p.verificationNote}</p><a href={`/authorities/${p.ref}/`}>Full text and source version</a></details>)}
<h2>Exam-source qualifications</h2>{exam.exams.map(e=><details class="rb-note"><summary>{e.unit.toUpperCase()} · {e.uncertainties.length} source qualifications</summary>{e.uncertainties.map(x=><p>{x.text}</p>)}</details>)}
<h2>All course records remain available</h2><p>{library.filter(r=>r.kind==='case').length} case records and {library.filter(r=>r.kind==='provision').length} legislation, treaty and other authority records are indexed across the site. The new library layers audited Torts dossiers over the original course information.</p><nav class="rb-actions"><a href="/cases/">Browse every case</a><a href="/statutes/">Browse every provision</a><a href="/sources/">Read the originals</a></nav></Layout>
